Differential equations, boundary data and a solvable flow model (@fd-mathematical-methods: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../../thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE", #source "../sources/Intermediate-Fluid-Mechanics-Liburdy.lingua#r_45KKWKB7DTN9MMQ951P62JHH5N", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P", #fluid-dynamics "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H") { r_5HKW1NTEG39SPQQ5PF9THNHCMX
**Read:** [Differential Equations — MIT 18.03SC](../../thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE), complete relevant ordinary-differential-equation and modal units; [Intermediate Fluid Mechanics — James Liburdy](../sources/Intermediate-Fluid-Mechanics-Liburdy.lingua#r_45KKWKB7DTN9MMQ951P62JHH5N), mathematical development alongside its flow problems; [Advanced fluid dynamics — Mei notes and MIT modules](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P), scaling, approximation and analytical solution methods.

Identify the unknown fields and their equations before choosing a solution method. A steady ordinary differential equation for a pipe profile and an unsteady partial differential equation for a velocity field need different data. Boundary and initial conditions supply physical information that a governing equation alone does not contain.

Work the needed units on ordinary differential equations, eigenmodes and numerical approximation in [Differential Equations — MIT 18.03SC](../../thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE). Derive one solution by integration, one by a similarity variable and one by separation into modes. Explain how constants are fixed and how a limiting case checks the result. For a nonlinear model, discuss existence, multiplicity and the chosen solution branch.

State what is prescribed at every boundary and which quantities are outcomes. Prescribing pressure and normal velocity independently at an incompressible outlet can overconstrain a problem. A solver returning a field is not proof that the mathematical or physical boundary-value problem was well posed.

**Continue:** [Mass and component balances — account for every stream](../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H).

